## What changed from PodFetch, and what Podsift added

CHANGES.md has the full list. In short: the Rust backend (`crates/`, `src/`,
`migrations/`) is unchanged and runs from the official pinned image. The bundled React
UI (`ui/`) keeps PodFetch's listening, subscription and playlist code, changed for
navigation, the player, settings and build tooling. Everything else — the transcript
workspace, briefs, cuts, Smart Play, flashcards, voice notes, private feeds, the "Worth
hearing" digest, and the companion service and MCP server that provide them — is new
code written for Podsift.

## Third-party components carried in the built images

- FFmpeg (the companion image copies the static build from the official PodFetch image),
  licensed GPL-3.0. See https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html.
- The bundled demo pack (`demo/`) is Hacker Public Radio content, CC BY-SA 4.0 per
  episode; see `demo/LICENSE-CONTENT.md` for attribution and per-episode licence checks.

Every other dependency is pulled from its own package registry at build time under its
own license (see `Cargo.lock`, `ui/pnpm-lock.yaml`, `companion/requirements.txt`,
`mcp/pyproject.toml`); none of their source is vendored into this repository.

Sponsor skipping uses Podsift's own transcript-derived detector, without SponsorBlock
API or database data. The imported Apache-2.0 PodFetch source retains its optional
SponsorBlock client and preference storage. Podsift's player does not read those
third-party timings, and the shipped image/Compose defaults disable external lookups.
